Subject: [PATCH 8/9] port: back shared memory with ictrobot_shm_v1

An anonymous mapping is private to its instance: every spawned child
gets an independent copy, and nothing cooperates. Back the main
segment and POSIX dynamic shared memory with shm_open objects overlaid
through the ictrobot_shm_v1 extension, so independently instantiated
guests see the same pages. The import namespace, pointer-width
selection and errno conversion live in the extension's own header
rather than being duplicated here: the server depends explicitly on
the extension, and its platform code only uses the typed C wrapper
from ictrobot_shm_v1.h.

